# Auto Package After Code Changes

When modifying application source code in this repository (C#, XAML, assets used by the app, installer script, etc.):

1. After changes compile successfully, **always** build the installable exe without asking the user.
2. Run publish + Inno Setup in sequence:

```powershell
dotnet publish "NaiwaProxy.csproj" -c Release -r win-x64 --self-contained true -p:PublishSingleFile=true -p:IncludeNativeLibrariesForSelfExtract=true -o "publish\win-x64"
& "C:\Program Files\InnoSetup6\ISCC.exe" "installer\NaiwaProxy.iss"
```

3. Tell the user the output path: `dist/Nexora-Setup-{version}.exe` (read version from `NaiwaProxy.csproj` or `installer/NaiwaProxy.iss`).

Skip packaging only when the user explicitly says not to, or when changes are docs-only / non-buildable and cannot affect the exe.
